  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dynetics obligated $1.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Dynetics received 39 awards for a current-year average award size of $28.9M. Obligations were up 77.1% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B to Dynetics in FY2026 to date, while the National Aeronautics and Space Administration and the General Services Administration obligated $8.4M and $2.8M respectively. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market for Dynetics with $870M in obligations, followed by Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $221M. Dynetics also shows R&D and engineering markets, including Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $12.8M and Engineering Services at $11.1M. The historical obligations trend shows FY21 at $420M, FY22 at $178M, FY23 at $117M, FY24 at $137M, FY25 at $636M, and FY26 at $1.1B. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Dynetics federal obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $1.1B in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $8.4M and the General Services Administration obligated $2.8M. Other agencies account for the remaining federal obligations for this partial fiscal year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets drive Dynetics federal revenue?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the top market with $870M in obligations. Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing follows with $221M, and smaller shares appear in R&D and engineering, including $12.8M for Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) and $11.1M for Engineering Services."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Dynetics make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Dynetics obligated $1.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Dynetics received 39 awards this fiscal year with an average award size of $28.9M. Historical obligations by fiscal year were $420M in FY21, $178M in FY22, $117M in FY23, $137M in FY24, and $636M in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Dynetics?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $1.1B to Dynetics in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $8.4M and the General Services Administration obligated $2.8M in the same period."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Dynetics sell to the government?",
      "a": "Dynetics sells primarily missile and space systems and related parts. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounts for $870M in obligations and Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $221M. Dynetics also has obligations in Research and Development and Engineering Services, including $12.8M and $11.1M respectively."
    },
